The '''Tapuya national football team''' ({{Lang-vol|Seleción de Tapuya}}) represents [[Tapuya]] in men's international association football. It is governed by the [[Tapuya Football Federation]] and competes as a member of the Mesogean Football Association within the [[AFA]] confederation.

Tapuya are currently ranked 38th in the [[AFA Men's World Ranking]] and qualified for their second [[AFA World Cup]] at the [[2022 AFA World Cup|2022 tournament]].

== History ==

=== Early development ===
Tapuya's football culture developed alongside the broader Volisanian-speaking world, with the domestic league benefiting from close ties to clubs in Volisania and Balisca. The Tapuya Premier League, founded in 1987, has produced several players who moved to larger Mesogean leagues.

=== World Cup appearances ===
Tapuya qualified for their first World Cup in 2014, exiting at the group stage but earning a draw against a higher-ranked opponent. The 2022 qualification marks the country's second appearance, with a squad featuring a mix of domestic talent and diaspora players from Volisanian and Baliscan clubs.

